WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.950
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.940
happening all the time,

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.950
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.570
to test for ourselves.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.540
Eco Styler is the brand
of gel I use all the time,

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.690
and I never knew it had
this Unicorn Glitter Gel.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.265
It's a translucent pink color

00:00:14.265 --> 00:00:16.206
with blue iridescent sparkles.

00:00:16.206 --> 00:00:17.400
It's so pretty.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.630
Running this through my hair,

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.210
I feel like you don't really
get the glittery effect.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.090
It just kind of tinted my
hair this bluish color,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.050
which is cool,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.420
just not what I thought
it was going to look like.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.868
I definitely saw the
glitter and color better

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.760
when I applied it to
brushed-back straight hair.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.980
I think this is cute for
a little glitter moment

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.030
every once in a while.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.550
And it actually washed
out of my hair easily.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.660
I don't know if you guys know this,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.010
but I'm a nail-polish freak.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.860
So when I saw Dew by Jinsoon going viral,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.420
I bought it immediately.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.310
This is a milky-white polish.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.560
It's very sheer and soft.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.210
My nails are super stained right now,

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.920
so I was worried about how it was looking

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.330
after the first coat,

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.010
but when I went in with that second coat,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.030
it looked really pretty,

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.010
and my nails looked so much better.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.900
It was a little streaky in the first coat,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.120
but the second went on totally smooth.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.030
I do wish, though, that
this had a flat paddle brush

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.150
instead of this brush just
to make it easier to paint.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.520
I'm sure you could find a really good

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.880
drugstore dupe for this polish,

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.500
because it is on the pricey side,

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.820
but I really like it.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.310
This is the new Urban Decay Vice Lip Bond

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.720
glossy liquid lipstick.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.760
So you get the glossiness of a lip gloss

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.500
and the wear of a liquid lipstick.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.240
This is extremely pigmented.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.740
I was really impressed by the color,

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.465
but I feel like it wasn't as shiny

00:01:27.465 --> 00:01:28.865
as I thought it would be.

00:01:28.865 --> 00:01:30.450
I let it dry down for 10 minutes

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.620
and kissed the back of my hand

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:32.940
to see if it transferred at all,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.710
and it did, but only a little bit,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.480
and the lipstick still looked good.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.642
It's actually very
similar to the Maybelline

00:01:38.642 --> 00:01:40.830
Vinyl Ink lip color I tried a while ago,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.682
so I would probably recommend that one,

00:01:42.682 --> 00:01:45.090
since it's cheaper and performs the same.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.760
I am not a pot-concealer kind of person,

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.410
but I was really excited to try out

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.660
this REM Beauty Sweetener concealer.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.660
I also got the Dreamcloud
blender to test out as well.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.251
I scooped some up and just warmed it

00:01:56.251 --> 00:01:58.551
on the back of my hand.
Then I used my fingers

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.020
to apply everywhere I wanted to conceal.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.510
The concealer looks thicker than it feels.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.915
I was actually surprised
at how lightweight it felt

00:02:05.915 --> 00:02:07.350
when I was blending it out.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.360
The coverage with this is amazing.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.730
I was so shocked at
how much it covered up.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.230
You don't need a lot at all.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.730
I definitely put too much on,

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.440
but I really, really like this.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.177
They also included a black and white shade

00:02:18.177 --> 00:02:20.342
in this concealer, so you
can lighten your shade

00:02:20.342 --> 00:02:21.780
or deepen it, which is cool.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.460
I also really like this little sponge,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.470
but it's not worth $15.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.930
These NYX Ultimate Glow
Shots look so pretty

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.640
that I literally bought three of them.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.290
They're supposed to be brightening

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.240
and give a really glowy effect.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.950
Although these are gorgeous in the tube,

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.470
they're just really
inconsistent on the eyes.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.836
The pigment on some is better than others,

00:02:39.836 --> 00:02:41.452
but overall, I would say the pigment

00:02:41.452 --> 00:02:42.960
isn't great with these on their own.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.285
I had to build them up a lot

00:02:44.285 --> 00:02:45.668
to get them to look like this.

00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:47.730
They definitely work better as a topper

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.170
over other eye shadows.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.990
I'm so torn on these
because they look so good,

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.390
but it takes a lot of
work to get them that way.

